WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:20.324
spent the first few minutes at the gym stretching—and feeling sorry for herself.

2
00:00:20.344 --> 00:00:25.586
"It's not fair that Jordan gets all the attention and money," she thought.

3
00:00:25.606 --> 00:00:29.668
"Meanwhile I get stuck with Jordan's hand-me-downs!"

4
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:36.323
But as Riley's body slowly warmed up, she could feel her mind calm down.

5
00:00:37.484 --> 00:00:40.405
Jordan's accident had been a nightmare for the whole family.

6
00:00:41.286 --> 00:00:48.310
Poor Jordan had pain all the time, and she couldn't ride Riley suddenly felt embarrassed.

7
00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.132
She'd probably sounded like a spoiled brat to her father.

8
00:00:53.093 --> 00:00:58.676
She knew she'd have to apologize, even though a small, bitter lump still sat in her stomach.

9
00:01:00.176 --> 00:01:04.399
Riley glanced at the clock, deciding to test her ankle on a stationary bike.

10
00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:09.803
As she headed toward the bike room, she glanced into a small workout room.

11
00:01:09.823 --> 00:01:13.105
"That's Quinn," Riley thought.

12
00:01:13.965 --> 00:01:14.946
"What's she doing?"

13
00:01:16.107 --> 00:01:20.069
She watched Quinn run forward and throw herself onto a floor mat.

14
00:01:24.452 --> 00:01:26.013
she practicing a fall?"

15
00:01:26.714 --> 00:01:27.534
Riley wondered.

16
00:01:28.215 --> 00:01:29.636
She watched Quinn do it again.

17
00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.903
"She's falling all wrong," Riley muttered.

18
00:01:36.923 --> 00:01:39.165
"She's going to get hurt."

19
00:01:40.386 --> 00:01:41.707
Riley pushed open the door.

20
00:01:41.727 --> 00:01:44.470
"Hey, Quinn."

21
00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.832
"Oh, hi.

22
00:01:47.572 --> 00:01:48.293
What do you want?"

23
00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:50.515
Quinn didn't sound mean.

24
00:01:50.955 --> 00:01:55.279
She just looked puzzled by Riley's sudden appearance.

25
00:01:55.299 --> 00:01:56.821
"I saw you practicing a fall."

26
00:01:58.702 --> 00:02:00.404
Quinn nodded, her face brightening.

27
00:02:01.268 --> 00:02:05.329
"I saw a video online that showed how to fall off a bike safely, and I've been practicing

28
00:02:05.349 --> 00:02:05.729
at home.

29
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.030
But I had to stop when I broke a lamp in the living room.

30
00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:11.031
My mom told me to practice here."

31
00:02:11.951 --> 00:02:12.731
Riley laughed.

32
00:02:12.751 --> 00:02:18.133
"I smashed a couple of photo frames at my house learning to fall."

33
00:02:18.153 --> 00:02:19.933
"Watch this!"

34
00:02:20.554 --> 00:02:23.795
Quinn crouched, and then sprang up and ran down the mat.

35
00:02:25.995 --> 00:02:31.378
She took a small leap, stretched out her hands, and did a strange handspring-like roll.

36
00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:35.641
do you think?"

37
00:02:36.161 --> 00:02:36.762
Quinn asked.

38
00:02:36.782 --> 00:02:40.264
"Um Riley hesitated.

39
00:02:40.284 --> 00:02:45.288
"I don't know who made that video, but you probably shouldn't fall like that."

40
00:02:47.129 --> 00:02:48.610
Quinn put her hands on her hips.

41
00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.271
"Why not?"

42
00:02:51.232 --> 00:02:54.234
Riley tried to remember how Jordan had explained it to her.

43
00:02:55.375 --> 00:03:00.571
Jordan was a great teacher, one who could correct Riley's mistakes without making her feel silly.

44
00:03:00.591 --> 00:03:05.655
"When you're falling, your instinct is to throw out your hands as you go down.

45
00:03:06.596 --> 00:03:09.318
But you should never put out your hands to break your fall."

46
00:03:09.338 --> 00:03:11.219
"That doesn't make sense."

47
00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:12.520
Quinn frowned.

48
00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.023
"I know it sounds weird," Riley said.

49
00:03:16.043 --> 00:03:21.628
"But if you reach out like that, your hands will take the weight of your falling body."

50
00:03:23.228 --> 00:03:27.829
Riley dropped onto her knees and threw out her hands to show Quinn what she was talking about.

51
00:03:27.849 --> 00:03:34.791
"The force of hitting the ground moves up your arm until it finds a weak spot, and breaks

52
00:03:34.911 --> 00:03:38.092
it. Most of the time that weak spot is your wrist.

53
00:03:39.092 --> 00:03:41.713
It could also be your elbow or even your collarbone.

54
00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:43.754
So don't use your hands."

55
00:03:43.774 --> 00:03:46.254
"Then what am I supposed to use?"

56
00:03:46.274 --> 00:03:49.675
"You're supposed to tuck your arms into your body.

57
00:03:50.235 --> 00:03:52.016
Then you can roll with the fall."

58
00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.963
Riley put her arms to her sides and fell onto the mat, rolling forward.

59
00:03:56.983 --> 00:04:03.768
"This way the force of your fall is distributed around your whole body.

60
00:04:04.348 --> 00:04:05.649
You're less likely to get hurt."

61
00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:07.470
Quinn scowled.

62
00:04:08.011 --> 00:04:09.792
"That's not what the guy says on the video.

63
00:04:10.112 --> 00:04:15.356
He says—" "He's giving out bad advice," Riley interrupted.

64
00:04:15.376 --> 00:04:19.399
"My sister is a great rider, and she taught me that fall."

65
00:04:19.419 --> 00:04:25.811
"Yeah, I've heard all about Miss Know-it-All Jordan," Quinn said, rolling her eyes.

66
00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:30.995
"I'm surprised you take advice from someone who crashed and can't even ride anymore."

67
00:04:32.075 --> 00:04:33.396
Riley's cheeks flamed.

68
00:04:33.416 --> 00:04:35.958
"Don't talk about my sister that way!

69
00:04:36.398 --> 00:04:40.361
She knows more about riding than some stupid guy on some stupid online video."

70
00:04:40.381 --> 00:04:45.584
"Thanks for your uh, help," Quinn said sarcastically.

71
00:04:45.604 --> 00:04:47.186
"I'm out of here."

72
00:04:48.126 --> 00:04:50.568
She grabbed her workout bag and glared at Riley.

73
00:04:52.568 --> 00:04:57.331
"You're pretending to be nice, but I can tell what you're really doing—trying to sabotage me for the

74
00:04:57.391 --> 00:05:03.135
tryout!" Quinn marched out of the room, slamming the door so hard the glass rattled.

75
00:05:08.419 --> 00:05:09.820
her?" Riley muttered.

76
00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.921
"I was just trying to help."

77
00:05:14.063 --> 00:05:15.724
The rest of the week passed quickly.

78
00:05:16.644 --> 00:05:21.728
Riley apologized to her father and tried to push the unpleasant scene with Quinn out of her mind.

79
00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:28.202
Quinn definitely got under Riley's skin, but the tryout was tomorrow, and Riley had to focus.

80
00:05:29.443 --> 00:05:34.985
That night after dinner Riley wheeled her bike out of the garage and began her pre-race prep.

81
00:05:36.166 --> 00:05:40.328
She started at the top of the bike, checking the shifters to make sure they were tight.

82
00:05:42.689 --> 00:05:44.849
Then she checked the brakes and the brake pads.

83
00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:50.452
She made sure the seat height was right and tightened the bolts so the seat wouldn't wiggle.

84
00:05:52.924 --> 00:05:54.225
Next she oiled the chain.

85
00:05:57.307 --> 00:06:02.109
Jordan had shown Riley how to replace the foam grips on the handlebars with tape a few weeks

86
00:06:02.169 --> 00:06:04.591
back, and now the tape was starting to fray.

87
00:06:05.691 --> 00:06:10.394
Riley pulled new tape out of her tool kit, and then stood there, trying to remember how to

88
00:06:10.454 --> 00:06:10.854
wrap it.

89
00:06:10.874 --> 00:06:12.835
"Need some help?"

90
00:06:13.596 --> 00:06:16.117
Jordan asked from the doorway, leaning on her crutches.

91
00:06:17.338 --> 00:06:18.539
Riley held out the tape.

92
00:06:18.559 --> 00:06:22.801
"Yeah, I can't remember how you did this."

93
00:06:22.821 --> 00:06:24.863
"I'll see what I can do."

94
00:06:25.924 --> 00:06:30.428
Riley grabbed a folding chair from a shelf in the garage, and Jordan sat on it with a

95
00:06:30.488 --> 00:06:40.156
sigh. can't wait to get off these crutches," she murmured, unwrapping the old tape from Riley's bike.

96
00:06:40.176 --> 00:06:42.858
"Maybe next month."

97
00:06:44.259 --> 00:06:49.644
Riley watched her sister remove the old tape and expertly wind new tape around the handlebars.

98
00:06:53.157 --> 00:06:56.599
"Tape is so much better than those foam grips," Jordan said.

99
00:06:56.619 --> 00:06:58.840
"It looks cooler too."

100
00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:02.082
"Much cooler," Riley agreed.

101
00:07:02.102 --> 00:07:03.423
"What's next?"

102
00:07:04.163 --> 00:07:06.624
Jordan looked the bike over with an expert eye.

103
00:07:06.644 --> 00:07:08.445
"Tire pressure and the treads?

104
00:07:09.486 --> 00:07:10.707
Have you tested the brakes?

105
00:07:10.967 --> 00:07:11.607
How's your helmet?

106
00:07:11.627 --> 00:07:12.167
Any cracks?"

107
00:07:13.388 --> 00:07:14.249
Riley smiled.

108
00:07:14.889 --> 00:07:17.750
She used to get annoyed when Jordan checked up on her like this.

109
00:07:18.791 --> 00:07:21.777
Now, before the tryout, it felt reassuring.

110
00:07:21.797 --> 00:07:25.160
"All good," Riley said.

111
00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:28.243
"I'm going to do a quick ride through the neighborhood.

112
00:07:29.404 --> 00:07:30.685
Tell Mom I'll be back soon."

113
00:07:31.525 --> 00:07:33.908
She strapped on her helmet and flew down the street.

114
00:07:37.951 --> 00:07:41.574
Riley tested the bike's gears and brakes as she rode the familiar streets.

115
00:07:44.737 --> 00:07:48.100
She turned onto a long street and leaned down, picking up speed.

116
00:07:49.064 --> 00:07:51.946
She felt a twinge in her ankle, but nothing serious.

117
00:07:52.607 --> 00:07:54.648
Confident, she put more weight on it.

118
00:07:54.668 --> 00:07:57.970
"It feels fine," Riley thought happily.

119
00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:02.533
She hoped her ankle—and the rest of her—felt this strong tomorrow.
